      "rdfs:comment": "Mass fraction of oxygen in dry air - a textbook value, not measured in this room. Follows from the standard mole fractions (O2 20.946 %, N2 78.084 %, Ar 0.934 %, CO2 0.041 %) and the molar masses, giving a mean molar mass of 28.97 g/mol: 0.20946 x 31.999 / 28.97 = 0.2314.",
